    "title": "pandas.Timestamp.fold — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1662.g0c49719283 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Timestamp.fold#\n\n- Timestamp.fold#\n- Return the fold value of the Timestamp. The fold attribute is used to disambiguate wall times in a repeated interval during daylight saving time transitions. \n  - Returns:\n    - int\n    - The fold value of the Timestamp, where 0 indicates the first occurrence of the ambiguous time, and 1 indicates the second.\n See also \n  - `Timestamp.dst`\n  - Return the daylight saving time (DST) adjustment.\n  - `Timestamp.tzinfo`\n  - Return the timezone information associated.\n Examples >>> ts = pd.Timestamp(\"2024-11-03 01:30:00\") >>> ts.fold 0",
    "markdown_length": 581,
